# The near tier, and the two things it has to get right at once.
#
# `Beta#render` is `Alpha#render` with one more call in the chain — the
# copy-paste-then-tweak that the exact tier cannot see and the semantic tier
# would need a paid summary to guess at. It must be found.
#
# `Gamma#render` reuses several of the same method names but does different
# work. It must not be. Without a control like this, a threshold low enough to
# catch Beta looks identical to a threshold that catches everything.
#
# The `dupes` verb asserts the WHOLE report, exact and near tiers together, so
# this also pins that Beta is reported ONCE — as near-structural — and not
# again by the exact tier.
dupes  Alpha#render+Beta#render
